<title>USA: TENNIS-ATP CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-ATP CHAMPIONSHIPS RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MASON, Ohio 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the $2.3</p>
<p>million ATP Championships on Wednesday (prefix number denotes</p>
<p>seeding):</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>1-Pete Sampras (U.S.) beat Justin Gimelstob (U.S.) 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>2-Michael Chang (U.S.) beat Wayne Ferreira (South Africa) 6-7</p>
<p>(4-7) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>3-Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia) beat Daniel Nestor (Canada) 4-6</p>
<p>7-5 7-6 (8-6)</p>
<p>5-Thomas Muster (Austria) beat Fabrice Santoro (France) 6-3</p>
<p>5-7 6-4</p>
<p>6-Sergi Bruguera (Spain) beat Scott Draper (Australia) 7-6</p>
<p>(8-6) 6-2</p>
<p>7-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) beat Chris Woodruff (U.S.) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-3) 7-6 (8-6)</p>
<p>9-Marcelo Rios (Chile) beat Thomas Johansson (Sweden) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>10-Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil) beat Todd Woodbridge (Australia)</p>
<p>3-6 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>Martin Damm (Czech Republic) beat 12-Richard Krajicek</p>
<p>(Netherlands) 6-4 7-6 (7-3)</p>
<p>14-Albert Costa (Spain) beat Tommy Haas (Germany) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>16-Patrick Rafter (Australia) beat David Wheaton (U.S.) 3-6</p>
<p>6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Jiri Novak (Czech Republic) beat Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands)</p>
<p>6-3 6-2</p>
</text>
